10. Release Tracker Required RBAC Model

Release Tracker must eventually support three effective access levels.

Do not implement yet during this analysis.

First determine how these roles should map to the existing AIDLC authentication architecture.

Role 1 — Admin

Admin users can:

* Access Generate Report.
* Generate reports.
* Perform administrative refresh operations.
* Refresh deployment status.
* Send Teams notifications.
* Perform other explicitly administrative/state-changing actions.

Admin users can access all normal user functionality.

⸻

Role 2 — Developer

Developer users can:

* Access Review Commits.
* Access Release Readiness.
* Access Scan History.
* Access other normal Release Tracker pages.
* View report information.
* Perform the allowed developer-level actions.

Developer users must not:

* Access Generate Report.
* Perform admin-only refresh operations.
* Perform admin-only report-generation operations.
* Perform admin-only notification operations.

Developer users may perform the Review Commit Override action if that action is explicitly intended for the developer role.

⸻

Role 3 — General Viewer / Unassigned User

A user who successfully authenticates through SSO but does not belong to the Admin or Developer role should still be able to access the general application.

Viewer users can:

* View normal pages.
* View Release Readiness.
* View Review Commits.
* View Scan History.
* View available reports/data.

Viewer users must NOT:

* Access Generate Report.
* Use Review Commit Override.
* Perform administrative refresh actions.
* Send Teams notifications.
* Perform other state-changing/admin operations.

